WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.667 --> 00:00:03.936
Tanya, get rid of her.

00:00:04.003 --> 00:00:06.739
We decided you were
the tragic hero in the opera.

00:00:07.773 --> 00:00:09.676
TANYA MCQUOID-HUNT:
<i> How did I not see the signs?</i>

00:00:19.385 --> 00:00:21.420
In the end of last season,

00:00:21.454 --> 00:00:24.590 line:0%
Tanya is sitting with Greg
in the last episode,

00:00:24.623 --> 00:00:26.425
and he's talking about
his health issues,

00:00:26.458 --> 00:00:27.426
<i> and she says...</i>

00:00:27.893 --> 00:00:30.563
I've had every kind of treatment
over the years.

00:00:30.597 --> 00:00:34.100
Death is the last
immersive experience

00:00:34.367 --> 00:00:35.534
I haven't tried.

00:00:35.935 --> 00:00:38.738
And I was thinking it'd be
so fun to bring Tanya back

00:00:38.772 --> 00:00:40.873
because she's such
a great character.

00:00:40.906 --> 00:00:43.476
But maybe that's
the journey for her,

00:00:43.543 --> 00:00:46.579
<i> is like a journey to... death.</i>

00:00:46.612 --> 00:00:48.614
<i> And not that I really
 wanted to kill Tanya,</i>

00:00:48.648 --> 00:00:50.316
because I love her
as a character,

00:00:50.382 --> 00:00:51.984
and obviously, love Jennifer.

00:00:52.051 --> 00:00:54.654
But I just felt like, you know,
we're going to Italy.

00:00:55.454 --> 00:00:57.424
<i> She's such a kind of diva,</i>

00:00:57.457 --> 00:00:59.959
<i> larger-than-life
 female archetype.</i>

00:00:59.992 --> 00:01:03.595
It just felt like we
could devise our own

00:01:03.629 --> 00:01:07.333
operatic conclusion
to Tanya's life and her story.

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:09.803
(PANTING)

00:01:09.836 --> 00:01:12.171
-GREG HUNT: Tanya!
-Yeah. In a minute!

00:01:12.238 --> 00:01:15.941
I just think her dying
at the hands of someone else

00:01:15.975 --> 00:01:18.077
felt too tragic.

00:01:18.110 --> 00:01:21.180
It felt like she needed
to give her best fight back,

00:01:21.246 --> 00:01:24.350
<i> and that she, in a way,
 had some kind of victory</i>

00:01:24.417 --> 00:01:28.154
<i> over whoever was conspiring
 to get rid of her.</i>

00:01:28.187 --> 00:01:30.457
So it just made me laugh
to think like, she would like,

00:01:30.490 --> 00:01:32.791
take out all of these
cabal of killers,

00:01:32.825 --> 00:01:35.294
<i> and that after she
 successfully does that,</i>

00:01:35.327 --> 00:01:37.529
then she just dies
this derpy death.

00:01:37.596 --> 00:01:40.132
And I just felt like,
that's just so Tanya. (LAUGHS)

00:01:40.499 --> 00:01:41.935
You've got this.

00:01:42.368 --> 00:01:43.302
(GRUNTS)

00:01:43.335 --> 00:01:44.604
-(SLIPS, GASPS)
-(THUDS)

00:01:44.637 --> 00:01:46.005
(WATER SPLASHING)

00:01:47.706 --> 00:01:50.610
I think as far as like,
what happens to Greg

00:01:50.643 --> 00:01:54.714
and the conspiracy
of Tanya's death,

00:01:54.781 --> 00:01:57.783
it's possible that I think
Portia is scared enough

00:01:57.817 --> 00:01:59.218
to just leave it alone,

00:01:59.285 --> 00:02:01.887
<i> but the fact that all of those
 guys die on the boat,</i>

00:02:01.954 --> 00:02:03.790
<i> it feels like there's
 gotta be somebody</i>

00:02:03.823 --> 00:02:05.558
<i> who's gonna track it
 back down to Greg.</i>

00:02:05.625 --> 00:02:07.861
But maybe you'll have to wait
to find out what happens.

00:02:10.162 --> 00:02:11.297
<i> At the end of the show,</i>

00:02:11.330 --> 00:02:13.799
<i> you see
 the three generations of men,</i>

00:02:13.832 --> 00:02:15.668
and there's this
attractive woman who crosses,

00:02:15.702 --> 00:02:17.370
<i> and they all sort of
 gawk at her.</i>

00:02:17.403 --> 00:02:20.039
<i> You know, my hope is that
 Dominic does change,</i>

00:02:20.072 --> 00:02:23.243
but there is a little bit
in the texture of it that

00:02:23.309 --> 00:02:25.644
their relationship with women
is gonna always be fraught

00:02:25.677 --> 00:02:28.080
with this sexual desire.

00:02:28.147 --> 00:02:31.985
When she hugged me just now,
I got a little aroused.

00:02:33.352 --> 00:02:35.321
No, no, it's a natural reaction.

00:02:36.823 --> 00:02:37.723
He kissed me.

00:02:38.490 --> 00:02:41.026
But that was it, okay?
That was all.

00:02:41.060 --> 00:02:43.162
The question of like whether
Harper and Cameron

00:02:43.196 --> 00:02:44.664
did more than the kiss,

00:02:45.064 --> 00:02:47.734
I think probably,
that's just all that happened.

00:02:47.767 --> 00:02:48.868
At the same time,

00:02:49.368 --> 00:02:51.604
there's some time that
isn't completely accounted for.

00:02:51.671 --> 00:02:54.574
And I think that that's why
it's like eating at Ethan.

00:02:55.441 --> 00:02:56.676
Ethan comes to Daphne,

00:02:57.109 --> 00:02:59.512
and did they have some kind of
a dalliance on the island?

00:02:59.545 --> 00:03:01.080
<i> Or whatever happened,</i>

00:03:01.113 --> 00:03:04.016
it allows him to let go
of the jealousy

00:03:04.050 --> 00:03:05.852
that has been brewing with him.

00:03:06.419 --> 00:03:09.589
<i>And it kind of brings back that
 first kind of sexual charge</i>

00:03:09.622 --> 00:03:11.390
<i> that happens in the beginning
 of relationships</i>

00:03:11.424 --> 00:03:13.259
<i> and sometimes,
 fades away over time.</i>

00:03:13.559 --> 00:03:14.626
By the end, you're like,

00:03:15.194 --> 00:03:17.630
well maybe what Ethan and Harper
need was just a small dash

00:03:17.696 --> 00:03:19.966
of what Cameron and Daphne have.

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:21.601
Thanks for putting up with me.

00:03:22.268 --> 00:03:23.269
I love you.

00:03:23.869 --> 00:03:26.038
It feels like Cameron, to me,
is like one of those guys

00:03:26.072 --> 00:03:27.739
that's not really gonna change.

00:03:27.773 --> 00:03:28.774
(LAUGHS)

00:03:29.241 --> 00:03:31.144
<i> Some of the unspoken things
 between them,</i>

00:03:31.210 --> 00:03:34.447
you wonder if that's gonna
ultimately catch up with them.

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:36.582
It is somewhat
of a happy ending,

00:03:36.615 --> 00:03:39.619
<i> although there's dark clouds
 in the horizon too.</i>

00:03:42.221 --> 00:03:45.991
The first season kind of
highlighted money, and then,

00:03:46.058 --> 00:03:47.493
<i> the second season is sex.</i>

00:03:47.560 --> 00:03:48.828
<i> And I think the third season,</i>

00:03:48.894 --> 00:03:52.131
it would be maybe a kind of
satirical and funny look

00:03:52.165 --> 00:03:55.434
at death and eastern religion
and spirituality.

00:03:55.467 --> 00:03:57.803
And it feels like
it could be a rich tapestry

00:03:57.836 --> 00:04:01.241
<i> to do another round
 at</i> White Lotus.

